1
00:00:00,720 --> 00:00:11,360
Hey, I had an episode for this week that was going to release today, but given what's going on in my country right now, I feel like it's best to push it off for a week to make room for the voices that are desperately trying to be heard right now.

2
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:14,480
As a white guy who grew up in the suburbs of St.

3
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:31,680
Louis, Missouri, I am far from an authority on the subject of race and police brutality in America, and to be honest, it makes me really uncomfortable to talk about because I'm afraid that I'm going to say something wrong or accidentally promote something bad, but I think that silence is also a problem.

4
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:36,880
So I don't have a whole lot to say, but I will say this, black lives matter.

5
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:41,520
If you find that offensive or you don't understand why people are so upset, I understand.

6
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:47,920
That was me just a few years ago when a lot of this all started in Ferguson, Missouri right down the road from me.

7
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,880
I was very much in the camp of, look, I get something's wrong, but this is not the way to do that.

8
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:11,280
And thanks to a lot of long conversations with very patient co workers, I've had my eyes open to a very different America than the one that I gre can say is just try to listen.

9
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:19,360
Find black authors or bloggers or journalists or creators and watch movies, read on Twitter.

10
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:39,440
Just try to be silent and listen to what these people have to say because when you hear their stories, their experiences, the stuff that's happening all the time, it's deeply, deeply uncomfortable to realize that this is the America that you've lived in your whole life, or at least it was for me.

11
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:42,960
I'm definitely not an authority.

12
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:43,520
on this.

13
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:46,000
I'm not going to pretend to understand it all that well.

14
00:01:46,480 --> 00:02:00,480
